sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-collective-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "It has been hypothesized, and the authors adopt, that the ability of neurons to unify into a centralized self is an evolutionary pivot of earlier cell-communication strategies that first solved problems in anatomical morphospace, a domain also requiring information processing above the single-cell level.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Neural unification into a self is a pivot of earlier morphogenetic cell communication";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "McMillen P, Levin M, “Collective intelligence: A unifying concept for integrating biology across scales and substrates”, Communications biology (2024), doi:10.1038/s42003-024-06037-4; section “Introduction”. Scope: Evolution of nervous systems from non-neural bioelectric signalling in metazoans"
}
